# Line endings.
#
# The whole codebase is authored with LF (see .editorconfig), so LF is what the
# repository stores *and* what lands in the working tree. Without this, Git on
# Windows converts to CRLF on checkout, which makes every file look modified to
# the next contributor on a different platform and turns a one-line change into a
# whole-file diff.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Lock files and generated artefacts: still text, still LF, but never worth
# reading in a diff. Collapsing them keeps a pull request reviewable.
package-lock.json -diff linguist-generated
frontend/src/types/api.d.ts -diff linguist-generated
frontend/openapi.json -diff linguist-generated

# Alembic migrations are generated but MUST be reviewed - autogenerate cannot tell
# a column rename from a drop-plus-add, so these are deliberately left diffable.
backend/alembic/versions/*.py text

# Binary, so Git never attempts a merge or a diff on them.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
